spec ww13-void-label-removal: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# WW13, label arm. Both sessions REMOVE n:Flag. Label removal is a void primitive: a conflict it hits cannot be returned by the
# statement, so it is RECORDED on the transaction and must surface at COMMIT as a
# serialization conflict, applying nothing (F3, rmp #2354). A COMMIT that succeeds
# after a recorded conflict is a silently dropped write.

starting permutation: s1x s1c s2x s2c
step s1x: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) REMOVE n:Flag RETURN n.name AS name
name
----
"n" 
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2x: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) REMOVE n:Flag RETURN n.name AS name
name
----
"n" 
(1 row)
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: serialization conflict
final final: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) RETURN n:Flag AS flagged
flagged
-------
false  
